In axios/axios, starting from Axios v1.8.0 the `allowAbsoluteUrls` configuration attribute was introduced to control the use of absolute URLs (PR https://github.com/axios/axios/pull/6795), but it appears to be ignored in the `buildFullPath` call from the HTTP adapter at `lib/adapters/http.js` line 231 in commit `72acf759373ef4e211d5299818d19e50e08c02f8`. With Axios 1.8.1, Node.js 22.12.0 on Debian 5.10.226-1, using the `http` adapter, it is still possible to make requests to absolute URLs even when `allowAbsoluteUrls` is set to `false`: 

